# Local env — holds VITE_SUPABASE_* and VITE_BETA_PASSCODE.
# NOTE: .env is still *tracked* (committed before this entry existed), so this only
# stops a NEW .env from being added. To actually untrack it you also need
#   git rm --cached .env
# which is deliberately NOT done: there is no .env.example, so an untracked .env
# would leave a fresh clone / CI build with no Supabase config.
.env
.env.local
